* CABSRT14 - MEDIA EXTRACT SORT FOR THE TAPE DESPATCH
* MVT OS/360 SORT/MERGE FORM OF JCL/CTLCARDS/CABSRT14.
* THE TAPE IS WRITTEN IN CARRIER ORDER SO THAT ONE VOLUME CAN BE
* SPLIT BETWEEN CARRIERS AT THE BUREAU.  THE LABEL AND TRAILER
* RECORDS MUST STAY AT THE FRONT AND BACK, WHICH IS WHAT THE
* LEADING SORT KEY ON THE TYPE BYTE DOES.
*
* THE RULE THAT LEFT THIS CARD
*   THE OUTFIL OMIT OPERAND ON THE TYPE BYTE AND THE PACKED
*   AMOUNT AT 375 IS NOT CODED HERE.  THIS SORT HAS NO OUTFIL
*   STATEMENT.  THE E35 EXIT CABSXTAP NOW DROPS EVERY DETAIL
*   RECORD WHOSE AMOUNT IS ZERO AND LEAVES LABEL AND TRAILER
*   RECORDS ALONE.
*   THE TRAILER HASH WRITTEN BY CABFMT07 STILL INCLUDES THE
*   DROPPED RECORDS, SO THE BUREAU RECONCILIATION HAS NEVER TIED
*   EXACTLY AND THE TOLERANCE THEY APPLY WAS AGREED IN 1997.
*
* OPTION EQUALS IS NOT CODED - THIS SORT HAS NO OPTION
* STATEMENT.  THE THREE KEY FIELDS TOGETHER ARE UNIQUE ON THIS
* EXTRACT, SO THE ORDER OF EQUAL KEYS DOES NOT ARISE.
*
* WHICH DETAIL RECORDS REACH THE VOLUME IS NO LONGER READABLE
* FROM THIS CONTROL CARD.
 SORT FIELDS=(1,1,CH,A,15,14,CH,A,29,6,CH,A)
 RECORD TYPE=F,LENGTH=(400)
 MODS E35=(CABSXTAP,8192,SORTEXIT,N)
 END
